{:edb/db-before-t 2872 :edb/db-after-t 2873 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536185 50 #inst "2026-10-09T18:42:45.493Z" 13194139536185 true] [17592186119865 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387731 13194139536185 true] [17592186119865 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387738 13194139536185 true] [17592186119867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387745 13194139536185 true] [17592186387731 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387732 13194139536185 true] [17592186387731 1089 "q-126837" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387731 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536185 true] [17592186387731 1100 "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3},{t}^{2}-2⟩$ at the point where $t=3,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387731 1113 #uuid "ff8b7d1f-787a-5846-b2f9-a68bcb9d4f3d" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387731 1145 "At the point where $t=3,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(3)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(3)+u{r}^{′}(3),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨{3}^{3},{3}^{2}-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(3) & =⟨3(3)^{2},2(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=3$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387733 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387734 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387735 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387736 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387737 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1041 "selection" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387737 13194139536185 true] [17592186387732 1110 #uuid "727d0217-ff47-55c7-97e2-76ebbeb27bcf" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387733 1034 "⟨9,1⟩+u⟨27,6⟩" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387733 1111 #uuid "cfbc2e52-a663-5cb7-98b4-0305e5f6711f" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387734 1034 "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨9,7⟩" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387734 1111 #uuid "e9630d09-3e39-5ca5-a0cd-e5ccf0c0b813" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387735 1034 "⟨9,1⟩+u⟨9,7⟩" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387735 1111 #uuid "026a915b-4342-55ee-ac65-fa0cfbb756c4" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387736 1034 "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨14,6⟩" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387736 1111 #uuid "3c18be1c-75ea-5a56-96c5-929ff8dd2e86" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387737 1034 "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387737 1111 #uuid "2c422e92-660c-5616-b868-8ebcf95bf214" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387738 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387739 13194139536185 true] [17592186387738 1089 "q-32876" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387738 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536185 true] [17592186387738 1100 "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2}),$ valid for real values of $u?$" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387738 1113 #uuid "33bfb8ae-51e5-575a-aee2-202f3434e957" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387738 1145 "The point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t=-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t=0 \\\\ t=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=\\frac{3}{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{3}{2}).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\frac{3}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u\\,(\\pi \\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387740 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387741 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387742 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387743 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387744 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1041 "selection" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387742 13194139536185 true] [17592186387739 1110 #uuid "9e75698a-e910-5bed-b0ad-fb527a02771e" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387740 1034 "-i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,k)" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387740 1111 #uuid "6f1ed178-5cf5-5d83-a3bc-dfd7c8a21552" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387741 1034 "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,j)" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387741 1111 #uuid "6940bd89-4ab1-5c22-ac0d-fe0022283b39" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387742 1034 "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,j+\\,k)" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387742 1111 #uuid "3e3edef2-6cc6-5021-bee2-7a90f682335e" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387743 1034 "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(-\\pi \\,j-\\,k)" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387743 1111 #uuid "befbd5a4-c675-5da0-9912-b913adce33c8" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387744 1034 "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k)" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536185 true] [17592186387744 1111 #uuid "5e29cd53-1332-5338-9ca6-c391c313a8ea" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387745 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387746 13194139536185 true] [17592186387745 1089 "q-75524" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387745 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536185 true] [17592186387745 1100 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,t\\in [0,\\pi )$ find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are perpendicular." 13194139536185 true] [17592186387745 1113 #uuid "f1e2ae0c-272c-5ed9-a620-4462d5cc1c06" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387745 1145 "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\cdot ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) & =0 \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in [0,\\pi )$, the only solutions are $t=0$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩=⟨0\\,,\\,3⟩, \\\\ r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩=⟨1\\,,\\,0⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the points $(0,3)$ and $(1,0).$" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387747 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387748 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387749 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387750 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387751 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1041 "selection" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387747 13194139536185 true] [17592186387746 1110 #uuid "a25f1b88-efd6-5bc5-adff-d60834a59ef9" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387747 1034 "$(0,3)$ and $(1,0)$" 13194139536185 true] [17592186387747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536185 true] [17592186387747 1111 #uuid "b2ee5cbf